title: 'sp-arithmetic: add checked functions, fix saturating division-by-zero, and extend fuzzer coverage'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    **BREAKING**: `PerThing::saturating_reciprocal_mul`, `saturating_reciprocal_mul_floor`,
    and `saturating_reciprocal_mul_ceil` now require `N: Bounded` and return
    `Bounded::max_value()` when `self` is zero, instead of panicking. The removed
    `checked_saturating_reciprocal_mul*` methods are no longer needed; callers should use
    the saturating versions directly.

    Changes to `sp-arithmetic`:
    - `helpers_128bit.rs`: Added `checked_multiply_by_rational_with_rounding` with proper
      `ArithmeticError` return type. The existing `multiply_by_rational_with_rounding` now
      delegates to the checked version.
    - `per_things.rs`: Added `checked_*` versions of `square`, `mul_floor`, `mul_ceil`,
      and `from_rational_with_rounding` to the `PerThing` trait. Added `checked_int_div`
      and `checked_div_with_rounding`. Fixed `saturating_reciprocal_mul*` to return
      `Bounded::max_value()` on zero instead of panicking (previously UB/panic). Removed
      `checked_saturating_reciprocal_mul*` methods (saturating operations are infallible
      by definition). Fixed `checked_rational_mul_correction` error semantics and `PerU16`
      debug display.
    - `fixed_point.rs`: Added `try_into_perbill` and checked `from_rational_with_rounding`.
      Updated to use `multiply_by_rational_with_rounding` in `FromStr`.
    - `traits.rs`: `EnsureFixedPointNumber` wrappers (`ensure_from_rational`,
      `ensure_mul_int`, `ensure_div_int`) convert `Option` to `Result<T, ArithmeticError>`
      with `DivisionByZero` for zero divisors and `Overflow` for all other failures.
    - `rational.rs`: Added `checked_to_den` and `checked_lcm`. The existing `to_den` and
      `lcm` now delegate to the checked versions. Updated `checked_add` and `checked_sub`
      to use `ArithmeticError`.

    Changes to downstream callers:
    - `pallet-nomination-pools`: Callers adapted for `Option`-returning checked methods.

    Fuzzer coverage:
    - 8 new fuzzer modules covering checked arithmetic, rounding, conversions, and utility
      functions across `PerThing` and `FixedPointNumber` types, using BigInt/BigUint oracles
      for value verification.
crates:
- name: sp-arithmetic
  bump: major
- name: pallet-nomination-pools
  bump: patch
